/*
 * Precomputed Mel filterbank matrix, EXPORTED DIRECTLY from librosa.filters.mel()
 * with the exact parameters mfcc.py/logmel.py use for training (sr=16000, n_fft=512,
 * n_mels=40, fmin=20, fmax=4000, htk=True, norm='slaney').
 *
 * Fix: the previous compute_mel_filterbank() did not compute a Mel filterbank at all -
 * it summed abs(windowed_frame[b]) over raw TIME-DOMAIN samples indexed as if they were
 * frequency bins, with no FFT anywhere in the class. This header replaces that with the
 * real, training-matching filterbank so the firmware feature pipeline actually matches
 * what the model was trained on, rather than an ad hoc approximation that could silently
 * drift from Python (or never have matched it in the first place).
 *
 * Shape: [40][257] = [n_mels][n_fft/2 + 1]
 * SIH Problem Statement 26172
 */
